redfin 1245: SweetMesa waits (bounded) for sweetfpcd before answering a catacomb / identity command, kern.sweet_mesa_fwd_wait_ms (default 0)

After a reboot biometrickitd sent 64 LoadCatacomb at first unlock while sweetfpcd was not up; the kernel answered
0xe00002d8 (offline) and biometrickitd never loaded again: BiometricSupport loads the catacomb once per process
(handleFirstUnlock 0x1efa13c3c -> restoreAndSyncTemplates -> loadCatacomb), a failed loadCatacombForComponent:
clears the identity list, and the only in-process retry, checkCatacombForUser: from startMatchOperation:
(0x1efa0d72c), is skipped when identitiesCount is 0 (dsc8 BiometricSupport, ~/fpr2/bs/bs.dis).
With kern.sweet_mesa_fwd_wait_ms = N (0..60000), 15/49/56/65/66 and user 61/64 (not the kernel-only SWCM master)
wait up to N ms for a bridge client when none is open; only the calling thread sleeps (gM dropped), the bridge
open wakes every waiter. kern.sweet_mesa_fwd_wait_state: counters. 0 = fail at once, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvAC4dCbJuYfzxCtCk4D8
